{
 "thread": "asUYVgrOFtA",
 "subject": "How to set covariance equal to 1 between variables",
 "messages_listed": 5,
 "last_activity": "2019-04-24T21:51:57Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "KxJ8n8ksAwAJ",
   "from": "car...@ucn.cl",
   "author": "63d5c113494a32df",
   "date": "2019-04-12T17:40:24Z",
   "subject": "How to set covariance equal to 1 between variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div>Dear all,<div><br></div><div>I am new in lavaan. So, I wanted to ask for help.</div><div><br></div><div>I wanted to test that two variables (CA and SS) are distinct yet interrelated variables. So, I want to compare two models through a CFA. </div><div><br></div><div>MODEL1 &lt;- &#39;</div><div><div>CA =~ CA1 + CA2 + CA3 </div><div>SS =~ SS1 + SS2 + SS3 +SS4 + SS5 </div><div>&#39;</div></div><div><br></div><div>Whereas </div><div><div>MODEL2 &lt;- &#39;</div><div><div>CA =~ CA1 + CA2 + CA3 </div><div>SS =~ SS1 + SS2 + SS3 +SS4 + SS5 </div><div>CA ~~ 1*SS &#39;</div></div></div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p><font size=\"4\">With model 2, I am trying to set a covariation between the two variables that equaled one, representing one continuum (Lewis, 2002, p: 11 doi: <a href=\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/3069380?seq=1#metadata_info_tab_contents\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.jstor.org/stable/3069380?seq%3D1%23metadata_info_tab_contents&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423897442000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1YCSV73Rgqr-bh7zFSFvuh\">https://www.jstor.org/stable/3069380?seq=1#metadata_info_tab_contents</a>)</font></p><p><br></p><p><font size=\"4\">And then I wanted to compare the results of two CFA models through a Chi-squared test.</font></p><p><font size=\"4\">MODEL1.fit = cfa(MODELO1, data=DATAIND, <a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423897442000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0VgLfPIhPw13cPShUciPe1\">std.lv</a> = TRUE)</font></p><p><font size=\"4\"></font></p><p><font size=\"4\">summary(MODEL1.fit, fit.measures=TRUE, standardized = TRUE, rsquare = TRUE)</font></p><p><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p><font size=\"4\">MODEL2.fit = cfa(MODEL2, data=DATAIND, <a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423897442000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0VgLfPIhPw13cPShUciPe1\">std.lv</a> = TRUE)</font></p><p><font size=\"4\"></font></p><p><font size=\"4\">summary(MODEL2.fit, fit.measures=TRUE, standardized = TRUE, rsquare = TRUE)</font></p><p><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p><font size=\"4\">Anova (Model1, Model2)</font></p><p><br></p><p><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p><font size=\"4\">Is that this approach correct?</font></p><p><font size=\"4\">In advance thank you very much for your help.</font></p><p><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p><p><font size=\"4\"><br></font></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Y0c6KVBHBAAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2019-04-16T07:57:44Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to set covariance equal to 1 between variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p><span style=\"font-size:large\">Is that this approach correct?</span></p></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Yes, but use lower-case<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> anova()</font>, or the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> lavTestLRT() </font>function to access more arguments (usually only necessary with robust estimators).  The upper-case <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Anova() </font>function in the car package is designed for other tasks.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423897443000&amp;usg=AOvVaw02YWFxpbSWhstjKQ5zqz9H\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ElBW4qyTCwAJ",
   "from": "Carolina Rojas Cordova",
   "author": "63d5c113494a32df",
   "date": "2019-04-16T16:56:50Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to set covariance equal to 1 between variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Thank you very much Terrence!!!!.</font><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Can I ask you additional questions, </font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">The model included four factors. Two factors (B = participative control and C = participative monitoring) represent emergent of project management and the other two (E = directive control and F = directive monitoring) represent planned style of project management. And I want to test that they are distinct yet interrelated. (As I mentioned in my previous mail). </font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">So according to (Lewis, 2002) to test this hypothesis, I have to test the following:</font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><b><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">MODEL 1</font></b></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">- Each item was allowed to load only on the factor for which it was a proposed, and no correlations were permitted in the error structure.</font></p></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><font> - Factors were allowed to covary </font>within managerial activities (for example, participative (B) and directive control (E) were allowed to covary<span style=\"display:inline;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;background-repeat:no-repeat;color:inherit\">),</span> because we proposed emergent and planned styles as offering interrelated approaches to each<font> activity.</font><br></font></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">- Consistent with our conceptual framework, the two planned activities were allowed to covary, reflecting their tight coupling.</font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></p><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">MODEL1 &lt;- &#39;</font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">B =~ B1 + B2 + B3 </font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">C =~ C1 + C2 + C3 +C4 + C5 </font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">D =~ D1 + D2 + D3 </font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">E =~ E1 + E2 + E3 +E4 </font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> B~~ E <br></font></div></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> C~~ F </font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> B~~ C <br></font></div></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> E~~ F &#39;<br></font></div></div></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font><div><b><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">MODEL 2</font></b></div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;line-height:normal\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Model 2 adds constraints to model 1. Specifically, we set the covariations between activities equal to one. These constraints signify that contrasting approaches comprise a single construct— for instance, that participative (B) and directive (E) control are two ends of the same continuum.</font></p></div><div><b><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></b></div><div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">MODEL2 &lt;- &#39;</font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">B =~ B1 + B2 + B3 </font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">C =~ C1 + C2 + C3 +C4 + C5 </font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">D =~ D1 + D2 + D3 </font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">E =~ E1 + E2 + E3 +E4 </font></div></div></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">B ~~ 1*E </font></div></div></div></div></div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">C ~~ 1*F </font><div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> B~~ C <br></font></div></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> E~~ F</font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">&#39;</font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">and then we use the anova as you suggested.</font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">I really appreciate your time, patience, and help!</font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Best,</font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Carolina </font></div><div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\" size=\"4\"><br></font><div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">El mar., 16 abr. 2019 a las 3:57, Terrence Jorgensen (&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tjorge...@gmail.com</a>&gt;) escribió:<br></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p><span style=\"font-size:large\">Is that this approach correct?</span></p></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Yes, but use lower-case<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> anova()</font>, or the<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> lavTestLRT() </font>function to access more arguments (usually only necessary with robust estimators).  The upper-case <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">Anova() </font>function in the car package is designed for other tasks.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423897446000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2giGji-CKWDFMVkrelpD8j\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">-- <br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lavaan+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>Visit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423897446000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2GVHKKpy0HN0ykN4CpZJUo\">https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan</a>.<br>For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423897446000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3a14AhnbJd_YfQeh8qZFIQ\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
