    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">B ~~ 1*E </font></div></div></div><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">C ~~ 1*F </font><div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> B~~ C <br></font></div></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> E~~ F</font></div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>You additionally need to constrain correlations consistent with this hypothesis that B and E are the same variable, and that C and F are the same variable.  In other words, there is only 1 correlation between those 2 variables ({BE} with {CF}):</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">label</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C <br>B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">label</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">F<br><br>E</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">label</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">F<br>E</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">label</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C</span></div></code></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br></div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792423897449000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1oZJaF43jjmG_yzgImbehv\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
